  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>]</mo></math> denote the greatest integer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The number of points where the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is not continuous is _____ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>]</mo></math>&nbsp;is discontinuous at integers so we will check at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;only&nbsp;</p><p>at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>we have&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LHL</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#183;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>RHL</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#183;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> Continuous at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Again at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>[</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LHL</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#183;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>RHL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi>LHL</mi></math></p><p>Hence, discontinuous at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Again at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>[</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>We have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LHL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>RHL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8800;</mo><mi>LHL</mi></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Hence, discontinuous at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Hence, discontinuous at exactly <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> points</p>",
